{
  "manufacturer": "Swegon",
  "manufacturer_slug": "swegon",
  "model": "SILVER C / SILVER RX rotary heat exchanger controller (Modbus RTU)",
  "model_slug": "silver-rx-rotary-heat-exchanger-control",
  "short_model": "SILVER RX rotor control",
  "aliases": [
    "SILVER RX heat exchanger controller",
    "SILVER C RX rotor drive",
    "DRHX",
    "SILVERCModbusHX"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Air handler (rotary heat exchanger drive controller)",
  "applies_to": "The rotary heat exchanger (rotor) drive controller in Swegon SILVER C RX air handling units, per sheet SILVERCModbusHX.201115.",
  "summary": "SILVER C RX air handling units use a separate controller to drive the rotary heat recovery wheel. It is a Modbus RTU slave with coils for start/stop, alarm reset and settings, discrete inputs for rotor-guard and drive alarms, input registers for output, motor and rotor speed, current, power, temperature and versions, and holding registers for the speed set point, speed limits, ramps and alternative communication settings.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 79,
    "baud": 38400,
    "parity": "None",
    "data_bits": null,
    "stop_bits": 1,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "0-based",
    "note": "Each table prints a register reference (0x0001, 1x0001, 3x0001, 4x0001) and an Address column one lower (0, or 0x0000 in hex). The Address column is the wire address: 4x0001 Setpoint is holding address 0."
  },
  "default_word_order": null,
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "Modbus, rotary heat exchanger controls SILVER RX",
    "doc_number": "SILVERCModbusHX.201115",
    "revision_date": null,
    "url": "https://www.swegon.com/globalassets/digizuite/12064-en-silvercrx_modbus_other_en.pdf",
    "pages": "p. 3 (addressing, comm. settings, coils), p. 4 (discrete inputs), p. 5 (input registers), p. 6 (holding registers)"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Coil and discrete-input tables print the address in decimal and the register reference with a 0x/1x prefix in decimal (e.g. 0x0010 = address 9); input and holding tables print the address in hex.",
    "The last coil is printed with register '0xx17' and address 17; the address column is used.",
    "Page 2 has a second communication table (address 54, even parity, 2 stop bits); the 'Modbus addressing' section and the footnote on p. 3 both give ID 79, 38400 baud, no parity, 1 stop bit, which are used as defaults here.",
    "Intern Temp (range -50.00 to 150.00 °C) is typed INT16; the sheet does not state signedness.",
    "Footnote 4 on I Ripple is not printed in the sheet.",
    "All values are 16-bit; there are no 32-bit registers.",
    "Input registers printed 3x0020-3x0029 (MOC Boot SW, motor/rotor/user-data config variant and version, V DC Bus peak, V Motor peak) are left out: from that row on the sheet's hex Address column equals the register number instead of one lower (3x0020 is printed with 0x0014), so the wire address cannot be settled.",
    "Speed registers are listed at 0.01 rpm, which applies with coil 14 High speed resolution = 1 (factory setting); with coil 14 = 0 the resolution is 0.1 rpm."
  ],
